title:: CaosMIDIOut
summary:: MIDI output wrapper with channel and range validation.
categories:: CaosBox
related:: Classes/CaosMIDI, Classes/MIDIOut

description::
Wraps a link::Classes/MIDIOut:: backend, fixes its channel and validates MIDI
ranges. The backend is injectable, so the class can be tested without hardware.

classmethods::

method:: new
code::
m = CaosMIDIOut(MIDIOut.newByName("BassStation", "out"), 1);
m.noteOn(48, 100);
m.noteOff(48);
::

instancemethods::

method:: noteOn
method:: noteOff
Send notes with 0..127 range. Velocity is preserved.

method:: cc
Sends a control change with controller and value in 0..127.

method:: program
Sends a program change.

method:: bend
Sends pitch bend in 0..16383.

method:: allNotesOff
Sends CC 123 (all notes off) on the wrapper channel.

method:: connect
method:: disconnect
Linux only. Creates or removes the ALSA/JACK connection from the SuperCollider
output port to a destination index. code::CaosMIDI.out:: does this
automatically on Linux.

